    "https://fa-ewca-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/3007": {
      "title": "Transfer Officer",
      "description": "Closing Date: 23/10/2026 Department: UMPI Registrar Category: Academic Student Services JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Presque Isle, ME, United States The University of Maine at Presque Isle (UMPI) is seeking to hire two (2) Transfer Officers . The Transfer Officers will evaluate domestic and foreign transcripts to determine course equivalencies, process transfer credit evaluations, maintain transfer credit data in the Student Information System, verify transcript authenticity and institutional accreditation, and serve as a resource on transfer policies for the University community. These are full-time, on-campus positions. For a complete list of responsibilities and qualifications, please review the full job description . The salary for these full-time, on-campus positions is $45,300.32 annually. The University will consider the salaries of current University of Maine System employees for transfer or promotion opportunities based on skills and experience. Benefits include medical, dental, vision, retirement, and tuition waiver programs for employees and eligible dependents. The University of Maine System is a recipient of the Wellness Councils of America’s Well Workplace Award and offers a variety of wellness programs. Visit our benefits website to learn more. Required Qualifications: Associate degree required; bachelor's degree preferred. The education requirement may be waived on a year-for-year basis for candidates with substantial post-secondary transfer credit experience. Excellent interpersonal skills for working with students, faculty, and staff. Excellent oral and written communication skills. Strong analytical, decision-making, and organizational skills. Proficiency with computers and databases. Preferred Qualifications: Experience in a student records environment. How to apply Materials must be submitted via “Apply Now\" below or visit the UMPI Careers Page . For application to be considered complete you must create an applicant profile (application) and submit ALL of the following: Cover letter Resume Important Information About the Recruitment Process: Applications will be reviewed on an ongoing basis. For full consideration, applications must be received by October 23,2026 . Applications received after this date may be reviewed at the discretion of the University. Finalist candidates will be asked to provide a list of professional references. A background check will be conducted for the selected candidate. Please note: The University is unable to consider applicants who require visa sponsorship. About the University For more than a century, the University of Maine at Presque Isle (UMPI) has helped students build successful professional careers. UMPI offers life-changing opportunities in a caring, small-university environment for 3,000 traditional and non-traditional students from Maine, across the United States, and around the world. To learn more, visit the University of Maine at Presque Isle website . Situated on 150 acres amidst the rolling hills and potato fields of northern Maine, UMPI strives to be the region’s premier learning institution while helping to stimulate cultural and economic development throughout Aroostook County and the State of Maine. Serving as an educational and cultural center for the area, university facilities host lectures, academic programs, concerts, dance performances, art exhibits, and plays that benefit the entire region. You can also explore community resources and regional attractions by reading more about what Aroostook County has to offer . Equal Opportunity Statement -The University of Maine System (the System) is an equal opportunity institution committed to fostering a nondiscriminatory environment and complying with all applicable nondiscrimination laws. Consistent with State and Federal law, the System does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, transgender status, gender, gender identity or expression, ethnicity, national origin, citizenship status, familial status, ancestry, age, disability (physical or mental), genetic information, pregnancy, or veteran or military status in any aspect of its education, programs and activities, and employment. The System provides reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. If you believe you have experienced discrimination or harassment, you are encouraged to contact the System Office of Equal Opportunity and Title IX Services at 5713 Chadbourne Hall, Room 412, Orono, ME 04469-5713, by calling 207.581.1226, or via TTY at 711 (Maine Relay System). For more information about Title IX or to file a complaint, please contact the UMS Title IX Coordinator at www.maine.edu/title-ix/ . Clery Act - The Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, or Clery Act, mandates that all Title IV institutions, such as the University, prepare, publish and distribute an Annual Security Report, (ASR) and provide notice of the availability of the ASR to all prospective employees. This report consists of two basic parts: disclosure of the University’s crime statistics for the past three calendar years; and disclosures regarding the University’s current campus security policies. You may view the University’s Annual Security Report. If you have any questions, contact Safety and Security 111 Campus Center 181 Main St., Presque Isle, ME 04769 Phone: (207) 768-9580. "
    },
    "https://fa-ewca-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/3235": {
      "title": "Workforce Enrollment Specialist",
      "description": "Closing Date: 16/10/2026 Department: UMPI Executive Administration Category: External Affairs JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Presque Isle, ME, United States The University of Maine at Presque Isle (UMPI) is seeking a Workforce Enrollment Specialist to join a team providing proactive support to prospective learners, working adults, and regional employer partners. Serving as the primary point of contact for non-degree, certificate, and degree pathways, the Specialist guides students seamlessly through the admissions and enrollment process. This role collaborates closely with UMPI Admissions, Professional Academic Advisors, YourPace Student Success Coaches, Student Records, Student Financial Services, and Student Support Services to ensure a supported, high-quality learner transition. This position requires a student-focused, tech-literate professional with outstanding communication skills, high attention to detail, and an engaging demeanor. The successful candidate leverages strong organizational skills, diplomacy, and initiative to anticipate applicant needs and support prospective learners throughout their application journey. The work schedule and location for this position is fully remote with standard working hours of 8:00 AM – 4:30 PM EST (schedule flexibility may occur during peak admissions cycles). Training and institutional events may require occasional travel to the UMPI campus. For a complete list of responsibilities and qualifications, please review the full job description. The salary for this full-time position is $45,300.32. The University will take into consideration the salary of current UMS employees for transfer/promotion, depending on skills and experience. The University of Maine System offers a comprehensive benefits package including medical, dental, and vision insurance, retirement plans, paid time off, tuition benefits for employees and eligible dependents, professional development opportunities, and wellness programs. Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree preferred; candidates with an associate's degree combined with related experience in admissions, tutoring, counseling, customer service, or sales will be considered. Knowledge and Skills: Strong listening, written, and verbal communication skills. Ability to relate to a diverse pool of prospective students with tact, diplomacy, and discretion. Outgoing, positive manner with the ability to connect with, motivate, and inspire people. Basic computer skills including proficiency in MS Word, Excel, and Gmail. Proven experience working in multiple platforms simultaneously and utilizing communication technology (e.g., Zoom). Excellent organizational skills, high attention to detail to ensure accuracy, and the ability to manage multiple projects at once. Aptitude for anticipating applicant needs. Perseverance and ability to look at all details and resources available in order to support students through the application process. Flexibility to work both independently and as part of a team. Willingness to advocate for your own training needs in order to meet all requirements of the position within the timeline outlined during onboarding. Preferred Qualifications Related sales or marketing experience preferred. Related admissions and recruitment experience preferred. Technology Requirements for Remote Work Proof of a stable, reliable internet connection of not less than 25 Mbps is required. Hotspots are not acceptable for this position. A dedicated workspace that is free from distractions, allows for private phone and Zoom conversations with students, and maintains respect for confidentiality according to policy and FERPA regulations. This space must accommodate a full workstation that includes 2 monitors, docking stations, and other necessary equipment. Annual completion of a Remote Work Agreement Form. How to Apply Materials must be submitted via “Apply Now\" below or visit the UMPI Careers Page . For an application to be considered complete, applicants must create an applicant profile and submit all of the following: Cover letter Resume Important Information About the Recruitment Process Applications will be reviewed on an ongoing basis. For full consideration, applications must be received by 5:00p.m. (EST) on October 16, 2026 . Applications received after this date may be considered at the discretion of the University. Finalist candidates will be asked to provide a list of professional references. A background check will be conducted for the selected candidate. Please note: The University is unable to consider applicants who require visa sponsorship. About the University For more than a century, the University of Maine at Presque Isle (UMPI) has helped students build successful professional careers. UMPI offers life-changing opportunities in a caring, small-university environment for 3,000 traditional and non-traditional students from Maine, across the United States, and around the world. To learn more, visit the University of Maine at Presque Isle website . Situated on 150 acres amidst the rolling hills and potato fields of northern Maine, UMPI strives to be the region’s premier learning institution while helping to stimulate cultural and economic development throughout Aroostook County and the State of Maine. Serving as an educational and cultural center for the area, university facilities host lectures, academic programs, concerts, dance performances, art exhibits, and plays that benefit the entire region. You can also explore community resources and regional attractions by reading more about what Aroostook County has to offer . Equal Opportunity Statement- The University of Maine System (the System) is an equal opportunity institution committed to fostering a nondiscriminatory environment and complying with all applicable nondiscrimination laws. Consistent with State and Federal law, the System does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, transgender status, gender, gender identity or expression, ethnicity, national origin, citizenship status, familial status, ancestry, age, disability (physical or mental), genetic information, pregnancy, or veteran or military status in any aspect of its education, programs and activities, and employment. The System provides reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. Clery Act- The Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act requires Title IV institutions such as the University to prepare, publish, and distribute an Annual Security Report (ASR) and provide notice of its availability to all prospective employees. The report includes crime statistics for the past three calendar years and disclosures regarding current campus security policies. "
    },
    "https://fa-ewca-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/2266": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Psychology (Search Re-opened)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 23/10/2026 Department: UMPI C J and Sociology Category: Faculty JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Presque Isle, ME, United States (Search Re-Opened) The University of Maine at Presque Isle is seeking an on-campus tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor of Psychology beginning as soon as January 1, 2027 for an academic year (9 month) appointment. The typical work year for this position is September 1 - May 31 of each year. The successful candidate will primarily teach undergraduate courses in Psychology (area of expertise open). Candidates who can teach courses in clinical/counseling psychology as well as some courses in research methodology, biological psychology, or I/O psychology are preferred. Responsibilities will encompass course instruction and development, advising, engaging in campus and professional service, collaborating with colleagues at the University of Maine at Fort Kent, and fostering opportunities for undergraduate experiential learning. We seek a dedicated professional with a passion for teaching and a commitment to career growth. Based on the qualifications and experience of the successful applicant, the minimum salary for Assistant Professor is $64,711 and minimum salary for Associate Professor is $73,786, commensurate with education and experience. Benefits include a 10% employer contribution to the UMS retirement plan, medical, dental, vision, and tuition waiver programs for employees and dependents. Visit our benefits website to learn more. Key Responsibilities include (not limited to): Deliver a minimum of four courses, or equivalent, per semester at both introductory and advanced levels, employing a blend of traditional and innovative modalities (competency-based, online, hyflex, and/or in-person). Actively contribute to the academic community through campus and professional service endeavors. Assist in the development, instruction, and administration of the undergraduate psychology program. Develop initiatives that involve undergraduate students, potentially leading to field placements, independent projects, or conference presentations/publications. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Effective communication skills, both oral and written, with the ability to collaborate within the academic community and engage with external stakeholders; proficiency in utilizing innovative teaching methods and technology to enhance student learning experiences, including online instruction; willingness to travel occasionally. Required Qualifications: A doctoral degree in Psychology (PhD or PSYD) or a closely related field from an accredited institution. Doctoral candidates who are ABD and plan to defend their dissertation prior to January 2027 will be considered. Preferred : Background in Clinical/Counseling Psychology with an ability to teach/develop courses that will complement existing areas of faculty expertise. How to apply Materials must be submitted via “Apply Now\" below or visit the UMPI Careers Page . For application to be considered complete you must create an applicant profile (application) and submit ALL of the following: Cover letter Resume Transcripts Teaching Philosophy Important items to know about the recruitment process: Review of applications will begin on October 23, 2026 . Candidates selected to proceed to the final stages of the search process will be requested to provide a list of references. A background screening will be conducted for the successful candidate. The University is not able to consider applicants who require Visa sponsorship support. About the University For more than a century, the University of Maine at Presque Isle (UMPI) has helped students build successful professional careers. UMPI offers life-changing opportunities in a caring, small-university environment for 3,000 traditional and non-traditional students from Maine, across the United States, and around the world. To learn more, visit the University of Maine at Presque Isle website . Situated on 150 acres amidst the rolling hills and potato fields of northern Maine, UMPI strives to be the region’s premier learning institution while helping to stimulate cultural and economic development throughout Aroostook County and the State of Maine. Serving as an educational and cultural center for the area, university facilities host lectures, academic programs, concerts, dance performances, art exhibits, and plays that benefit the entire region. You can also explore community resources and regional attractions by reading more about what Aroostook County has to offer . Equal Opportunity Statement -The University of Maine System (the System) is an equal opportunity institution committed to fostering a nondiscriminatory environment and complying with all applicable nondiscrimination laws. Consistent with State and Federal law, the System does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, transgender status, gender, gender identity or expression, ethnicity, national origin, citizenship status, familial status, ancestry, age, disability (physical or mental), genetic information, pregnancy, or veteran or military status in any aspect of its education, programs and activities, and employment. The System provides reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. If you believe you have experienced discrimination or harassment, you are encouraged to contact the System Office of Equal Opportunity and Title IX Services at 5713 Chadbourne Hall, Room 412, Orono, ME 04469-5713, by calling 207.581.1226, or via TTY at 711 (Maine Relay System). For more information about Title IX or to file a complaint, please contact the UMS Title IX Coordinator at www.maine.edu/title-ix/ . Clery Act - The Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, or Clery Act, mandates that all Title IV institutions, such as the University, prepare, publish and distribute an Annual Security Report, (ASR) and provide notice of the availability of the ASR to all prospective employees. This report consists of two basic parts: disclosure of the University’s crime statistics for the past three calendar years; and disclosures regarding the University’s current campus security policies. You may view the University’s Annual Security Report. If you have any questions, contact Safety and Security 111 Campus Center 181 Main St., Presque Isle, ME 04769 Phone: (207) 768-9580. For more than a century, the University of Maine at Presque Isle has been helping students find their path to great professional careers providing its 1,300 traditional and non-traditional students from all areas of the state, country, and world with life-changing opportunities in a caring, small-university environment. Further information about the University of Maine at Presque Isle can be found at https://www.umpi.edu/ . The university sits on 150 acres surrounded by the rolling hills and potato fields of northern Maine and the university strives to be the region’s premier learning institution while helping to stimulate cultural and economic development in Aroostook County and the State of Maine. The university serves as an educational and cultural center for the area and its facilities are utilized for lectures, programs, concerts, dance performances, exhibits, and plays that benefit the entire region. Learn more about what Aroostook County has to offer here . "
    },
    "https://fa-ewca-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/2913": {
      "title": "Electrical Manager",
      "description": "Department: UMPI Physical Plant Admin Category: Skilled Trades (Electrical) JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Presque Isle, ME, United States The University of Maine at Presque Isle is seeking an Electrical Manager to oversee the safe, reliable, and efficient operation of campus electrical infrastructure. This leadership role manages electrical maintenance and repair projects, supervises electrical trades staff and contractors, coordinates with campus departments and project managers, and supports budgeting, purchasing, and inventory management. The Electrical Manager ensures compliance with all safety regulations while providing technical expertise for complex electrical systems and capital projects. This is an essential, hands-on position that requires the ability to work during campus emergencies and inclement weather, perform physically demanding tasks, and maintain a safe and productive work environment. The regular schedule is Monday through Friday, 7:00 a.m. to 3:00 p.m., with availability to assist with emergencies after hours. This position is designated as an essential position requiring the individual to be able to work during periods of inclement weather and/or campus emergencies. Why Join UMPI? Starting pay: $31.47/hour (or applicable transfer rate) Benefits package valued at 53% above base pay Free tuition for employees (up to 8 credits per semester) 65% tuition discount for spouse and dependents Medical, dental, vision, life, and disability insurance University retirement contributions 13 paid holidays plus vacation and sick leave Wellness rewards, confidential counseling, and employee discounts For a complete list of responsibilities and qualifications, please review the full job description . The starting pay for this full time, essential position is $31.47 or the appropriate transfer rate. The University of Maine System offers a wide range of benefits for employees including, but not limited to, tuition benefits (employee and dependent), comprehensive insurance coverage including medical, dental, vision, life insurance, and short and long term disability as well as retirement plan options. Required Qualifications: Valid Maine Master Electrician License Seven years of related electrical experience High school diploma or equivalent (additional experience may substitute) Valid Maine driver's license Ability to perform physically demanding work, including lifting up to 50 pounds How to Apply: Materials must be submitted via “Apply Now\" below or visit the UMPI Careers Page . For application to be considered complete you must create an applicant profile (application) and submit ALL of the following: Cover letter Resume Important items to know about the recruiting process: Applications will be reviewed on an ongoing basis and will remain posted until filled. Finalists will be required to provide contract information for three (3) professional references. We are unable to consider applicants who require visa sponsorship. Incomplete materials will not be considered. The successful applicant is subject to appropriate background screenings and post-offer physical. About the University For more than a century, the University of Maine at Presque Isle has been helping students find their path to great professional careers providing its 3,000 traditional and non-traditional students from all areas of the state, country, and world with life-changing opportunities in a caring, small-university environment. Further information is available on the University of Maine at Presque Isle website . The university sits on 150 acres surrounded by the rolling hills and potato fields of northern Maine and the university strives to be the region’s premier learning institution while helping to stimulate cultural and economic development in Aroostook County and the State of Maine. The university serves as an educational and cultural center for the area and its facilities are utilized for lectures, programs, concerts, dance performances, exhibits, and plays that benefit the entire region. Learn more about what Aroostook County has to offer. Equal Opportunity Statement- The University of Maine System (the System) is an equal opportunity institution committed to fostering a nondiscriminatory environment and complying with all applicable nondiscrimination laws. Consistent with State and Federal law, the System does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, transgender status, gender, gender identity or expression, ethnicity, national origin, citizenship status, familial status, ancestry, age, disability (physical or mental), genetic information, pregnancy, or veteran or military status in any aspect of its education, programs and activities, and employment. The System provides reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. If you believe you have experienced discrimination or harassment, you are encouraged to contact the System Office of Equal Opportunity and Title IX Services at 5713 Chadbourne Hall, Room 412, Orono, ME 04469-5713, by calling 207.581.1226, or via TTY at 711 (Maine Relay System). For more information about Title IX or to file a complaint, please contact the UMS Title IX Coordinator at www.maine.edu/title-ix/ . Clery Act- The Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, or Clery Act, mandates that all Title IV institutions, such as the University, prepare, publish and distribute an Annual Security Report, (ASR) and provide notice of the availability of the ASR to all prospective employees. This report consists of two basic parts: disclosure of the University’s crime statistics for the past three calendar years; and disclosures regarding the University’s current campus security policies. You may view the University’s Annual Security Report . If you have any questions, contact Safety and Security 111 Campus Center 181 Main St., Presque Isle, ME 04769 Phone: (207) 768-9580. "
    },
    "https://fa-ewca-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/3320": {
      "title": "Senior Graphic Designer",
      "description": "Closing Date: 30/10/2026 Department: UMPI Marketing and Communications Category: Media JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Presque Isle, ME, United States The University of Maine at Presque Isle (UMPI) is seeking a Senior Graphic Designer to serve as a creative leader and visual brand steward within a dynamic Marketing and Communications team. Reporting to the Director of Creative Services, the Senior Graphic Designer conceptualizes, designs, and produces high-quality, on-brand visual content across print, digital, web, social, and advertising channels that advances the University’s brand and supports enrollment, advancement, and institutional priorities. This role provides creative direction and mentorship to junior designers and student workers, and works closely with storytellers, copywriters, photographers, videographers, and colleagues across campus to translate strategic goals into compelling visual solutions. This position requires an experienced, self-directed designer with a strong portfolio, expert command of Adobe Creative Suite, and a thorough understanding of typography, layout, color theory, print production, and vendor coordination. The successful candidate brings original ideas to the table, leads projects from concept through final production with minimal supervision, and serves as a resource to faculty, staff, and campus partners on visual identity and design best practices. The work schedule and location for this position is fully remote with standard working hours of 8:00 AM – 4:30 PM EST (schedule flexibility may occur around project and campaign deadlines, occasionally including evenings or weekends). Training, campus events, and photo/video shoots may require occasional travel to the UMPI campus. For a complete list of responsibilities and qualifications, review the complete Senior Graphic Designer job description . The salary for this full-time position is $54,000.00. The University will take into consideration the salary of current UMS employees for transfer/promotion, depending on skills and experience. The University of Maine System offers a comprehensive benefits package including medical, dental, and vision insurance, retirement plans, paid time off, tuition benefits for employees and eligible dependents, professional development opportunities, and wellness programs. Learn more about University of Maine System employee benefits . Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree or certificate in graphic design, visual communication, or a related field; or an equivalent combination of education and experience. A minimum of five to seven years of professional graphic design experience, ideally including work in an agency, corporate, or higher education marketing setting, supported by a strong portfolio. Familiarity with the UMPI brand. Knowledge and Skills: Thorough understanding of design principles, typography, layout, color theory, and print production. Expert-level proficiency with Adobe Creative Suite (InDesign, Illustrator, Photoshop) and familiarity with digital and print content development tools. Demonstrated ability to generate original concepts, provide art direction, and lead design projects from concept through completion with minimal oversight. Experience developing and maintaining visual identity guidelines and ensuring consistent brand application across a wide range of materials. Strong organizational skills, high attention to detail, and the ability to manage multiple projects and competing deadlines simultaneously. Ability to work effectively with copywriters, photographers, videographers, and cross-departmental colleagues, and to be receptive to creative direction and constructive feedback. Flexibility to work both independently and as part of a team, with willingness to pursue additional training needed to meet the requirements of the position. Preferred Qualifications Experience designing for enrollment or recruitment marketing in a higher education setting. Experience with motion graphics, video editing, or web/UX design. Experience overseeing external vendors, printers, or freelance creative talent. Technology Requirements for Remote Work Proof of a stable, reliable internet connection of not less than 25 Mbps is required. Hotspots are not acceptable for this position. A dedicated workspace that is free from distractions, allows for private phone and video conversations, and maintains respect for confidentiality according to policy and FERPA regulations. This space must accommodate a full workstation that includes 2 monitors, docking stations, and other necessary equipment. Annual completion of a Remote Work Agreement Form. How to Apply Materials must be submitted via “Apply Now” below or through the UMPI Careers Page . For an application to be considered complete, applicants must create an applicant profile and submit all of the following: Cover letter Resume Portfolio or link to an online portfolio of design work Important Information About the Recruitment Process Applications will be reviewed on an ongoing basis. For full consideration, applications must be received by 5:00p.m. (EST) on October 30, 2026 . Applications received after this date may be considered at the discretion of the University. Finalist candidates will be asked to provide a list of professional references. A background check will be conducted for the selected candidate. Please note: The University is unable to consider applicants who require visa sponsorship. About the University For more than a century, the University of Maine at Presque Isle (UMPI) has helped students build successful professional careers. UMPI offers life-changing opportunities in a caring, small-university environment for 3,000 traditional and non-traditional students from Maine, across the United States, and around the world. To learn more, visit the University of Maine at Presque Isle website . Situated on 150 acres amidst the rolling hills and potato fields of northern Maine, UMPI strives to be the region’s premier learning institution while helping to stimulate cultural and economic development throughout Aroostook County and the State of Maine. Serving as an educational and cultural center for the area, university facilities host lectures, academic programs, concerts, dance performances, art exhibits, and plays that benefit the entire region. You can also explore community resources and regional attractions by reading more about what Aroostook County has to offer . Equal Opportunity Statement- The University of Maine System (the System) is an equal opportunity institution committed to fostering a nondiscriminatory environment and complying with all applicable nondiscrimination laws. Consistent with State and Federal law, the System does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, transgender status, gender, gender identity or expression, ethnicity, national origin, citizenship status, familial status, ancestry, age, disability (physical or mental), genetic information, pregnancy, or veteran or military status in any aspect of its education, programs and activities, and employment. The System provides reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. Clery Act- The Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act requires Title IV institutions such as the University to prepare, publish, and distribute an Annual Security Report (ASR) and provide notice of its availability to all prospective employees. The report includes crime statistics for the past three calendar years and disclosures regarding current campus security policies. "
    },
    "https://fa-ewca-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/3363": {
      "title": "Part-Time Faculty: Social Work (Remote)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 04/12/2026 Department: UMPI C J and Sociology Category: Temporary JobSchedule: Part time PrimaryLocation: Presque Isle, ME, United States Part-Time Faculty, Social Work (Remote) The University of Maine at Presque Isle ( UMPI) invites applications for a part-time faculty position in Social Work within the undergraduate Bachelor of Social Work program, beginning in the Spring 2027 semester. This is a remote position that will include synchronous zoom teaching. Courses a re delivered online in traditional 15-week semesters. Compensation is on a per-credit-hour basis, commensurate with qualifications and experience, and aligned with applicable collective bargaining agreements or institutional policies. Responsibilities Teach in the Bachelor of Social Work program, in the areas of preparatory practicum courses (Junior Field Seminar) and Human Behavior in the Social Environment. Use both synchronous and asynchronous teaching modalities. Maintain office hours and attend faculty meetings. Required Qualifications Master of Social Work from a CSWE-accredited program. Preferred Qualifications Doctorate (DSW) or PhD in social work or a related discipline. Technology Requirements: Part-time faculty must have appropriate technology to teach, grade, and participate in online meetings, including: Computer (laptop) with sufficient processing speed High-speed internet connection Webcam Microphone How to Apply Materials must be submitted via “Apply Now” below or through the UMPI Careers Page . You will need to create an applicant profile and upload: A cover letter describing your experience, interests, and suitability for the position, including the courses you could teach. Curriculum vitae (preferred) or résumé. Transcript for the highest degree earned. Important Information About the Recruitment Process Applications are due by December 4 2026, at 5:00 p.m. Eastern Time. Incomplete applications will not be considered. Materials received after the application deadline may be reviewed at the University’s discretion. Candidates selected for the final stages of the search will be asked to provide a list of references. A background screening will be conducted for candidates who advance in the process. The University is not able to consider applicants who require visa sponsorship. About the University For more than a century, the University of Maine at Presque Isle (UMPI) has helped students build successful professional careers. UMPI offers life-changing opportunities in a caring, small-university environment for 3,000 traditional and non-traditional students from Maine, across the United States, and around the world. To learn more, visit University of Maine at Presque Isle . Situated on 150 acres amidst the rolling hills and potato fields of northern Maine, UMPI strives to be the region’s premier learning institution while helping to stimulate cultural and economic development throughout Aroostook County and the State of Maine. As an educational and cultural center for the area, the university hosts lectures, academic programs, concerts, dance performances, art exhibits, and plays that benefit the entire region. You can also explore community resources and regional attractions by reading more about what Aroostook County has to offer . Equal Opportunity Statement- The University of Maine System (the System) is an equal opportunity institution committed to fostering a nondiscriminatory environment and complying with all applicable nondiscrimination laws. Consistent with State and Federal law, the System does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, transgender status, gender, gender identity or expression, ethnicity, national origin, citizenship status, familial status, ancestry, age, disability (physical or mental), genetic information, pregnancy, or veteran or military status in any aspect of its education, programs and activities, and employment. The System provides reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. If you believe you have experienced discrimination or harassment, you are encouraged to contact the System Office of Equal Opportunity and Title IX Services at 5713 Chadbourne Hall, Room 412, Orono, ME 04469-5713, by calling 207.581.1226, or via TTY at 711 (Maine Relay System). For more information about Title IX or to file a complaint, please contact the UMS Title IX Coordinator at www.maine.edu/title-ix/ . Clery Act- The Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, or Clery Act, mandates that all Title IV institutions, such as the University, prepare, publish and distribute an Annual Security Report, (ASR) and provide notice of the availability of the ASR to all prospective employees. This report consists of two basic parts: disclosure of the University’s crime statistics for the past three calendar years; and disclosures regarding the University’s current campus security policies. You may view the University’s Annual Security Report . If you have any questions, contact Safety and Security 111 Campus Center 181 Main St., Presque Isle, ME 04769 Phone: (207) 768-9580. "
    },
    "https://fa-ewca-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/2977": {
      "title": "YourPace Part-Time Faculty: Business",
      "description": "Closing Date: 07/11/2026 Department: UMPI CBE Adult Learner Category: Temporary JobSchedule: Part time PrimaryLocation: Presque Isle, ME, United States For more than a century, the University of Maine at Presque Isle has been helping students find their path to great professional careers providing its 1,300 traditional and non-traditional students from all areas of the state, country, and world with life-changing opportunities in a caring, small-university environment. The University of Maine at Presque Isle (UMPI) seeks dedicated subject matter experts for fully remote Adjunct Faculty positions in our YourPace competency-based education (CBE) Business Programs. YourPace offers asynchronous, flexible, student-centered degree programs serving adult learners. Teaching assignments run in eight-week sessions across six start dates throughout the year. We seek educators who are deeply committed to student success, higher education equity, and the unique mission of public regional institutions. YourPace Adjunct Faculty facilitate asynchronous online learning by proactively engaging self-paced adult learners, providing substantive feedback, and evaluating student competencies within established SLA timelines (typically 24–48 hours). Faculty are also responsible for active communication and participating in course maintenance or curriculum updates as assigned. UMPI values instructors who build genuine connections with students and prioritize quality teaching over high course loads. To be considered, your cover letter must include a 1–2 paragraph statement addressing: Your personal, professional, or academic connection to Maine, rural higher education, or UMPI’s mission. A brief breakdown of your current teaching load and active commitments at other institutions. Generic, automated mass-applications that omit this statement will be automatically filtered out during initial HR intake. Subject Matter Tracks Applicants must identify up to two (2) primary teaching tracks in their application cover letter. Undergraduate Discipline Clusters Track UG-1: Accounting, Finance & Quantitative Methods- Accounting, Finance, Investment, Micro/Macro-Economics, Business Mathematics Track UG-2: AI, Business Intelligence & Technology- Artificial Intelligence Management, Business Intelligence, Governance & Compliance Track UG-3: Leadership, HR & Organizational Behavior- Management, Leadership, Human Resources, Change Management, Ethics Track UG-4: Marketing & Professional Communication- Branding, Marketing, Social Media Marketing & Management, Professional Communication Track UG-5: Operations, Strategy & Sustainability- Project Management, Supply Chain Management, Strategic Thinking, Sustainability Graduate Discipline Clusters Track GRAD-1: Advanced Finance, Accounting & Strategy- Accounting & Finance, Investment & Strategic Thinking Track GRAD-2: AI, Analytics & Governance- (Artificial Intelligence Management, Business Intelligence & Analytics including Governance & Compliance Track GRAD-3: Leadership, HR & Managerial Communication- Change Management & Leadership, HR & Organizational Development, Professional & Managerial Communication Track GRAD-4: Marketing, Global Business & Administration- Branding & Marketing including Social Media, Global Business Management, Business Administration & Applications Track GRAD-5: Healthcare, Operations & Sustainability- Healthcare Management, Project & Supply Chain Management, Ethics & Sustainability, Corporate Social Responsibility Qualifications & Technology Requirement s Undergraduate Tracks: Master’s degree in Business or a related field from an accredited institution Minimum of 3 years of direct professional industry experience. Graduate Tracks: Doctorate in Business or a related field. Technology Requirements: Computer/laptop with modern processing capabilities, high-speed internet, webcam, and microphone. Preferred Qualifications : Prior higher education teaching experience (online/asynchronous preferred), experience with Competency-Based Education (CBE) assessment models, and capacity for active student engagement. Compensation & Working Conditions Adjunct faculty compensation and load limits are determined in accordance with the applicable University System Collective Bargaining Agreement (CBA) / Memorandum of Understanding (MOU) for Part-Time Faculty. Positions are non-tenure-track, fully remote, and scheduled on a course-by-course basis depending on student enrollment and program needs. How to Apply Click “Apply Now” below or visit the UMPI Careers Page . To ensure full consideration, submit your application via the UMPI Careers Portal with the following required documents : Cover Letter specifying up to two Track Codes and a 1–2 paragraph statement detailing your teaching commitments and connection to Maine, rural higher education, or UMPI’s mission. Curriculum Vitae (CV) or Résumé. Graduate Transcripts (unofficial copies acceptable for application) for your highest earned degree. Important items to know about the recruitment process: Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis, and candidates will be hired as programmatic needs arise. (Unless otherwise notified, applications will remain on file until May 30, 2027. If no communication regarding application status has been received by that date, the application will be considered inactive.) Incomplete applications or general submissions failing to address the screening prompts will not be considered. Candidates selected to proceed to the final stages of the search process will be requested to provide a list of references. A background screening will be conducted on candidates who move forward in the selection process. The University is not able to consider applicants who require Visa sponsorship support. Clery Act- The Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, or Clery Act, mandates that all Title IV institutions, such as the University, prepare, publish and distribute an Annual Security Report, (ASR) and provide notice of the availability of the ASR to all prospective employees. This report consists of two basic parts: disclosure of the University’s crime statistics for the past three calendar years; and disclosures regarding the University’s current campus security policies. You may view the University’s Annual Security Report . If you have any questions, contact Safety and Security 111 Campus Center 181 Main St., Presque Isle, ME 04769 Phone: (207) 768-9580 Equal Opportunity Statement - Equal Opportunity Statement- The University of Maine System is an equal opportunity institution committed to nondiscrimination. The following person has been designated to handle inquiries regarding non-discrimination policies: Director of Equal Opportunity, 5713 Chadbourne Hall, Room 412, University of Maine, Orono, ME 04469-5713, 207-581-1226. TTY 711 (Maine Relay System). "
    },
    "https://fa-ewca-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/3349": {
      "title": "Facilities Maintenance Worker CL1 (Third Shift)",
      "description": "Closing Date: 16/11/2026 Department: UMPI Physical Plant Admin Category: Facilities Maintenance JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Presque Isle, ME, United States The University of Maine at Presque Isle is seeking a full-time, regular, Facilities Maintenance Worker- CL1 (Custodian) to begin immediately. This is a third shift (overnight) position. If you take pride in a job well done and want steady employment with great benefits, we want to hear from you. On-the-job training is provided. Work Schedule: Wednesday through Sunday, 10:00 pm- 6:30 am (third shift). Wages: $18.33 per hour plus $0.80 shift differential, or the appropriate transfer rate for a current employee within the Service & Maintenance collective bargaining agreement. Benefits: This is a full-time position with a benefits package that can be worth up to 53% of your base pay. Benefits include: Health insurance: two medical plans through Anthem for you and your family, plus dental and vision plan options. Paid holidays: 13 paid holidays each year, including Thanksgiving and the day after, Christmas, and New Year’s Day. Paid time off: vacation time that grows with your years of service, plus sick time per year. Free college classes: free tuition for you (up to 8 credit hours per semester) at any University of Maine System campus, and 65% off tuition for your spouse and dependent children. Retirement plan: both you and the University contribute to your retirement account through TIAA. Life and disability insurance: University-paid life insurance (1 times your yearly pay) and University-paid long-term disability, with extra coverage available. Support for you and your family: free, confidential Employee Assistance Program, a wellness program with incentives, and group discounts on home, auto, and pet insurance. This position is designated as an essential position requiring the individual to be able to work during periods of inclement weather and/or campus emergencies. What you will do: Use cleaning equipment (such as vacuums and floor machines) and cleaning products safely. Lift and carry items that are sometimes heavy, such as trash, furniture, and equipment. Shovel snow from building entrances and walkways. Pick up trash and debris near the outside of buildings. Clean restrooms, classrooms, offices, hallways, and other spaces in and around campus buildings. Work on your own or as part of a team. Occasionally climb ladders up to 12 feet. Follow safety rules and report anything that is broken or unsafe. For a complete job description click here . Required Qualifications: High school diploma or GED Valid driver’s license, and able to be approved to drive University vehicles under the University’s Driver Administration Policy. Preferred Qualifications: Related cleaning experience Experience using commercial cleaning equipment HOW TO APPLY To apply, click “Apply Now\" below, or go to the UMPI Careers Page at umpi.careers.maine.edu . To apply, create an account and complete a short application. Uploading a resume and cover letter is encouraged; if they are not included, please provide specific details about your work history and education in your application. Need help applying? We are happy to help. Call UMPI Human Resources at 207-768-9479 (Monday through Friday, 8:00 am to 4:30 pm) or schedule an appointment online here . When you come in, a computer will be ready for you to use, and staff can walk you through the application. Important items to know about the recruitment process: Applications will be accepted through November 16, 2026. Candidates selected to proceed to the final stages of the search process will be requested to provide a list of references. A background screening and a pre-employment physical will be conducted for the successful candidate. The University is not able to consider applicants who require Visa sponsorship support. About the University For more than a century, the University of Maine at Presque Isle (UMPI) has helped students build successful professional careers. UMPI offers life-changing opportunities in a caring, small-university environment for 3,000 traditional and non-traditional students from Maine, across the United States, and around the world. To learn more, visit the University of Maine at Presque Isle website . Situated on 150 acres amidst the rolling hills and potato fields of northern Maine, UMPI strives to be the region’s premier learning institution while helping to stimulate cultural and economic development throughout Aroostook County and the State of Maine. Serving as an educational and cultural center for the area, university facilities host lectures, academic programs, concerts, dance performances, art exhibits, and plays that benefit the entire region. You can also explore community resources and regional attractions by reading more about what Aroostook County has to offer . Equal Opportunity Statement- The University of Maine System (the System) is an equal opportunity institution committed to fostering a nondiscriminatory environment and complying with all applicable nondiscrimination laws. Consistent with State and Federal law, the System does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, transgender status, gender, gender identity or expression, ethnicity, national origin, citizenship status, familial status, ancestry, age, disability (physical or mental), genetic information, pregnancy, or veteran or military status in any aspect of its education, programs and activities, and employment. The System provides reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. Clery Act- The Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act requires Title IV institutions such as the University to prepare, publish, and distribute an Annual Security Report (ASR) and provide notice of its availability to all prospective employees. The report includes crime statistics for the past three calendar years and disclosures regarding current campus security policies. "
    },
    "https://fa-ewca-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/3372": {
      "title": "Part-Time Faculty: History and Political Science",
      "description": "Closing Date: 13/11/2026 Department: UMPI CBE Adult Learner Category: Temporary JobSchedule: Part time PrimaryLocation: Presque Isle, ME, United States The University of Maine at Presque Isle (UMPI) is seeking to hire part-time Adjunct Faculty members who are subject matter experts in History and Political Science. The History and Political Science program supports online and in-person instruction, and is delivered in traditional 15-week semesters and/or 8-week Competency-Based Education (CBE) formats. All YourPace/CBE competencies are fully online and asynchronous, and interpersonal interactions with students are expected. Adjunct Faculty are compensated based on agreements as per the appropriate Collective Bargaining Agreements/MOU. Qualifications Minimum Qualifications Adjunct Faculty for undergraduate degree programs must have at minimum, a master’s degree from an accredited institution, and/or significant work experience in a related field. Adjunct Faculty for graduate degree programs must have a Doctorate, terminal, advanced degree in field of study, and/or significant work experience in a related field. Preferred Qualifications Experience teaching at the college-level Online teaching experience Teaching in a competency-based education model Technology Requirements : Adjunct Faculty are required to have the appropriate technology to teach in a fully online environment as appropriate. This includes, but is not limited to: Computer (laptop) with appropriate amounts of processing speed High-speed internet connection Webcam Microphone How to Apply Submit materials via “Apply Now” below or visit the UMPI Careers Page . You will need to create an applicant profile and upload: Cover letter describing your experience, interests, and suitability for the position, including the subjects you could teach. Curriculum vitae (preferred) or résumé. Transcript for the highest degree earned. Important Information About the Recruitment Process: Applications are reviewed on a rolling basis, and candidates may be hired as programmatic needs arise. Incomplete applications will not be considered. Materials received after the application deadline may be reviewed at the University’s discretion. Candidates selected for the final stages of the search will be asked to provide a list of references. A background screening will be conducted for candidates who advance in the process. The University is not able to consider applicants who require visa sponsorship. About the University For more than a century, the University of Maine at Presque Isle has been helping students find their path to great professional careers providing its 3,000 traditional and non-traditional students from all areas of the state, country, and world with life-changing opportunities in a caring, small-university environment. Further information about the University of Maine at Presque Isle can be found at https://www.umpi.edu/ The university sits on 150 acres surrounded by the rolling hills and potato fields of northern Maine and the university strives to be the region’s premier learning institution while helping to stimulate cultural and economic development in Aroostook County and the State of Maine. The university serves as an educational and cultural center for the area and its facilities are utilized for lectures, programs, concerts, dance performances, exhibits, and plays that benefit the entire region. Learn more about what Aroostook County has to offer here . Equal Opportunity Statement- The University of Maine System (the System) is an equal opportunity institution committed to fostering a nondiscriminatory environment and complying with all applicable nondiscrimination laws. Consistent with State and Federal law, the System does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, transgender status, gender, gender identity or expression, ethnicity, national origin, citizenship status, familial status, ancestry, age, disability (physical or mental), genetic information, pregnancy, or veteran or military status in any aspect of its education, programs and activities, and employment. The System provides reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. If you believe you have experienced discrimination or harassment, you are encouraged to contact the System Office of Equal Opportunity and Title IX Services at 5713 Chadbourne Hall, Room 412, Orono, ME 04469-5713, by calling 207.581.1226, or via TTY at 711 (Maine Relay System). For more information about Title IX or to file a complaint, please contact the UMS Title IX Coordinator at www.maine.edu/title-ix/ . Clery Act- The Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act, or Clery Act, mandates that all Title IV institutions, such as the University, prepare, publish and distribute an Annual Security Report, (ASR) and provide notice of the availability of the ASR to all prospective employees. This report consists of two basic parts: disclosure of the University’s crime statistics for the past three calendar years; and disclosures regarding the University’s current campus security policies. You may view the University’s Annual Security Report . If you have any questions, contact Safety and Security 111 Campus Center 181 Main St., Presque Isle, ME 04769 Phone: (207) 768-9580. "
    }
